---
description: Backend API conventions
globs: ["src/**/*.ts"]
---

- Stack: NestJS (TypeScript), Prisma + Postgres (Supabase), class-validator DTOs.
- Every endpoint must validate input with a DTO before touching the database
  — see roster/dto and auth/dto for the pattern. No raw request bodies
  passed to Prisma calls.
- Every new table needs a Prisma model added to prisma/schema.prisma and a
  migration — never hand-edit the schema directly against a running database.
- Roster matching logic lives ONLY in RosterService. AuthService calls it
  — auth does not reimplement matching logic (see auth.service.ts).
- Supabase is used only for OTP send/verify (SupabaseService). Do not use
  it for anything else without updating this rule and the build plan.
- Do not add new npm packages without flagging it in chat first.
- New modules follow the existing folder pattern: <name>/<name>.module.ts,
  <name>.controller.ts, <name>.service.ts, <name>/dto/*.dto.ts.
